      "text": "H(x)P−1 G(x)Y (x)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8205882352941176,
        "y0": 0.5484444444444445,
        "x1": 0.8250980392156863,
        "y1": 0.5610227272727273
      },
      "text": ".",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5011764705882353,
        "y0": 0.591020202020202,
        "x1": 0.8916094771241829,
        "y1": 0.6173876262626263
      },
      "text": "The main idea in this line of work is to ﬁnd P and Y (x) such that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5652957516339869,
        "y0": 0.6305176767676768,
        "x1": 0.8918071895424836,
        "y1": 0.6454179292929293
      },
      "text": "−Θ(x) − Θ⊤(x) > 0 ∀x ∈ Rn \\ {0}, (12)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5011764705882353,
        "y0": 0.6610202020202021,
        "x1": 0.891888888888889,
        "y1": 0.7566287878787878
      },
      "text": "for all systems (A,B) compatible with the data. In the earlier work [8], H(x) is taken to be equal to the identity matrix, which implies that Z(x) = F(x). In contrast, [9] considers more general Z(x) satisfying (10). This strategy is appealing because it leads to data-based linear matrix inequalities for control design. Unfortunately, however, the method also has some major limitations.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5064705882352941,
        "y0": 0.7702272727272728,
        "x1": 0.8917630718954248,
        "y1": 0.7984482323232324
      },
      "text": "(1) The matrix ∂Z∂x (x) must have full row rank for all x ∈ Rn \\ {0}.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.624686274509804,
        "y0": 0.7780454545454545,
        "x1": 0.6421372549019608,
        "y1": 0.7786515151515152
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "caption",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5517647058823529,
        "y0": 0.7998080808080809,
        "x1": 0.8918431372549019,
        "y1": 0.8123876262626263
      },
      "text": "Indeed, suppose that there exists a nonzero x",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5354901960784314,
        "y0": 0.8117436868686869,
        "x1": 0.8918022875816993,
        "y1": 0.8399621212121212
      },
      "text": "such that ∂Z∂x (x) does not have full row rank. Then Θ(x) is singular, which implies that (12) does not",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6080196078431372,
        "y0": 0.8195606060606061,
        "x1": 0.6254705882352941,
        "y1": 0.8201666666666667
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "caption",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5354901960784314,
        "y0": 0.8413232323232324,
        "x1": 0.8919084967320261,
        "y1": 0.9092058080808081
      },
      "text": "hold. Note that the full row rank condition can only hold if p ≤ n, i.e., the number of polynomials in Z is less than or equal to the state-space dimension of the system. This limits the class of Lyapunov functions of the form (11) that can be considered by the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4750996732026144,
        "y0": 0.946929292929293,
        "x1": 0.4832385620915033,
        "y1": 0.9595075757575757
      },
      "text": "4",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
